UPDATE companies SET description='Countryside Amish Furniture operates from Arthur, Illinois, where owner Mel Stutzman purchased the business in 2010 after more than 25 years working in Amish furniture shops. Raised Amish with formal schooling ending at eighth grade, Stutzman progressed from sanding to finish room to shop foreman before moving into custom cabinetry. The company remains family-owned and operated, drawing on Stutzman’s direct experience to vet partner workshops.

The retailer offers made-to-order solid wood furniture across dining, office, bedroom, living room, nursery, and outdoor categories, with thousands of designs spanning Traditional, Farmhouse, Mission, Shaker, and Contemporary styles. Production is distributed among more than 100 family-run Amish workshops in Pennsylvania, Indiana, and Ohio. Customers select from North American hardwoods — oak, cherry, brown maple, tiger maple, walnut — and choose stains, fabrics, leathers, or Sunbrella outdoor textiles. Each piece is built with mortise-and-tenon, dovetail, and tongue-and-groove joinery, hand-sanded, and finished with catalyzed conversion varnish. Countryside coordinates the process, provides free material samples, and ships finished goods to the contiguous 48 states for a flat $150 fee that includes in-home placement and assembly.

Orders are split with half due at the shop and half at finishing, and lead times typically run 14 to 18 weeks.

Stutzman’s hands-on background drives the quality standards: he inspects hidden surfaces, requires solid hardwood for structural components, and insists on cut joinery that accommodates seasonal wood movement. The sales team maintains high-touch communication throughout the build, updating clients until delivery.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and personalization", "Order management and production coordination with Amish workshops", "Finish and material sampling program", "White-glove delivery and on-site assembly", "Trade program for design professionals", "Mortise-and-tenon joinery", "Dovetail drawer construction", "Tongue-and-groove panel and case back joinery", "Hand sanding of all surfaces", "Catalyzed conversion varnish finishing"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Contract furniture (trade)"], "materials": ["Solid North American hardwood (Oak, Cherry, Brown Maple, Tiger Maple, Walnut)", "Catalyzed conversion varnish", "Fabrics", "Leathers", "Sunbrella outdoor fabrics", "Poly colors"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "14 to 18 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100+ family Amish workshops across Pennsylvania, Indiana, and Ohio", "Solid hardwood construction with mortise-and-tenon, dovetail, and tongue-and-groove joinery", "Catalyzed conversion varnish finish for durability", "Free wood, stain, fabric, and leather samples by mail", "Flat $150 white-glove delivery and on-site assembly in contiguous 48 states", "Half payment at shop, half at finishing"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Arthur, Illinois -> db", "Family-owned and operated -> /", "Owner Mel Stutzman -> /", "Mel Stutzman raised Amish, former shop foreman -> /about-us", "Purchased Countryside in 2010 -> /about-us", "25+ years in furniture and cabinetry -> /about-us", "100+ family Amish workshops in Pennsylvania, Indiana, Ohio -> /about-us", "Materials: Solid North American hardwood, catalyzed conversion varnish finish -> /about-us", "Lead time: 14 to 18 weeks -> /about-us", "Delivery: Flat $150, carried inside, placed, set up, contiguous 48 states -> /about-us", "Payment: Half at shop, half at finishing -> /about-us", "Free wood, stain, fabric, leather samples by mail -> /about-us", "Workshop selection criteria: solid hardwood, named joinery, hand sanding -> /about-us", "Product categories: dining, office, bedroom, living room, baby & kids, outdoor -> /", "Styles: Traditional, Farmhouse, Mission, Shaker, Queen Anne, Contemporary/Modern, French Country, Rustic & Live Edge -> /", "Wood types: Oak, Cherry, Brown Maple, Tiger Maple, Walnut -> /", "Finishes: Stains, Fabrics, Leathers, Outdoor Colors & Fabrics, Poly Colors, Sunbrella Outdoor Fabrics -> /", "Customization: comprehensive personalization possibilities, modify designs -> /", "High-touch sales team, updates during build, ship and assemble on-site -> /", "Ship entire contiguous U.S. -> /", "Handcrafted by Amish -> /", "Sustainable sourcing and building -> /", "Trade Program -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Who builds it: 100+ family Amish workshops in Pennsylvania, Indiana, and Ohio", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='countryside-amish-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Creative Hi-Tech Ltd. (CHTL) operates a 25,000-square-foot facility in Schaumburg, Illinois. The company was founded in 1998, beginning with a single pick-and-place machine in a 7,000-square-foot building. Over the following decades it expanded to two production lines equipped for both surface-mount and through-hole technology, adding advanced inspection and test equipment.

The shop provides full-service printed circuit board assembly, from quick-turn prototypes to high-volume production runs. Capabilities include SMT, PTH, and mixed-technology assembly; BGA and micro-BGA placement down to 0201 pitch; lead-free and RoHS-compliant processes; box-build and system integration; wire harness and cable assembly; and rework and repair. In-house testing covers AOI, X-ray, and flying-probe inspection. The facility also supports PCB design, fabrication, and turnkey procurement.

Customers span aerospace, military, medical, and electronic industrial products, as well as agricultural, automotive, pharmaceutical, wireless, telecommunication, defense, satellite, industrial electronics, computer, and business electronics sectors. Named references include Honeywell and several LED lighting manufacturers.

The company emphasizes flexibility, taking orders as small as a single board, and promotes a secure, cloud-based workflow for BOM upload and digital build-data validation. ITAR registration and compliance with UL, CSA, FDA, and IPC standards are cited as differentiators, along with rapid lead times ranging from one day for quick-turn work to four to eight weeks for standard production.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR','RoHS','UL','CSA','FDA','IPC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB assembly", "PCB prototyping", "Quick-turn PCB assembly", "Box build assembly", "Wire harness & cable assembly", "Turnkey PCB assembly", "Surface mount (SMT) assembly", "Through-hole (PTH) assembly", "Mixed technology assembly", "BGA and micro-BGA assembly", "Lead-free assembly", "PCB rework and repair", "PCB design", "PCB fabrication", "SMT stencils", "AOI inspection", "X-ray inspection", "Flying probe inspection", "Fine pitch placement (0201)", "Testing & inspection", "Cloud-based BOM upload", "Digital build data validation", "Secure data handling"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Military", "Medical", "Electronic Industrial Products", "Agricultural", "Automotive", "Pharmaceutical", "Wireless", "Telecommunication", "Defense", "Satellite", "Industrial Electronics", "Computer", "Business Electronics"], "materials": ["FR-4", "FR-5", "CEM-1", "CEM-3", "Copper", "Rogers (RF)", "High Tg materials", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Pick and place machines", "SMT equipment", "PTH equipment", "AOI", "X-Ray", "Flying probe inspection machines", "Two production lines"], "volume": "Prototype to high volume production runs", "lead_time": "Quick turn: 1-15 days; standard: 4-8 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Free ground shipping on prototypes and quick-turn orders (25 pieces or less)", "Free PCB tooling on 2-layer assemblies (100 pieces or less)", "ITAR registered facility", "25,000 sq. ft. plant with two SMT/PTH production lines", "Quick-turn lead times as fast as 1 day"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998 -> /about-us", "25,000 sq. ft. facility in Schaumburg, IL -> /, /about-us", "Started with one pick-and-place machine in 7,000 sq. ft. building -> /about-us", "Two production lines, SMT and PTH equipment -> /, /about-us", "Services: PCB assembly, prototyping, quick turn, box build, wire harness, cable assembly, rework, BGA, micro-BGA, mixed technology, lead-free, turnkey -> /, /services, /capabilities", "Industries served: aerospace, military, medical, electronic industrial products, agricultural, automotive, pharmaceutical, wireless, telecommunication, defense, satellite, industrial electronics, computer, business electronics -> /, /services, /capabilities", "Customer references: Honeywell, LED lighting manufacturers -> /", "ITAR registered -> /services", "RoHS, UL, CSA, FDA, IPC compliance -> /services", "Materials: FR-4, FR-5, CEM-1, CEM-3, copper, Rogers (RF), high Tg, aluminum -> /services", "Volume: prototype to high volume, orders as small as one board -> /about-us, /capabilities", "Lead times: 1 day to 4-8 weeks -> /", "Equipment: pick and place, AOI, X-ray, flying probe -> /services, /capabilities", "Secure cloud-based workflow, digital build data validation -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Creative Hi-Tech Ltd. (CHTL) is renowned for being a leading PCB assembly services provider. We offer our assembly services for single as well as multi-layer PCBs. We provide the complete range of services from design to delivery.", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='creative-hi-tech' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Creative Packaging Company is headquartered in Shelbyville, Kentucky, just outside Louisville. The business has operated for over three decades as a privately held, family-run enterprise. While no founding year is published, the company describes its history as spanning more than thirty years of providing custom-designed packaging solutions.

The company manufactures expanded polystyrene (EPS) products, gel packs, and liners, including its signature BioDrain environmentally safe disposal gel pack. Operations center on a 140,000-square-foot manufacturing facility on 26 acres in Shelbyville, supplemented by five to seven additional plants across the United States. The workforce numbers around 300 employees, serving roughly 300 customers nationwide. Capabilities include custom EPS molding, gel pack production, cold chain management programs, temperature and material testing, and environmental consulting for packaging.

Primary markets include meal kit delivery services, pharmaceutical and life sciences distribution, protective packaging, construction, and other temperature-sensitive distribution sectors. The firm works directly with manufacturers and distributors in those industries, providing both standard and custom-engineered packaging systems.

Creative Packaging emphasizes its family-owned structure and ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system as differentiators. The national footprint of multiple manufacturing sites is positioned to support rapid, reliable cold chain logistics, while the BioDrain product addresses environmental disposal concerns. The company states it forms partnerships with customers to deliver cost-effective, high-performance packaging solutions.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Expanded polystyrene (EPS) molding", "Gel pack manufacturing", "Custom packaging design and engineering", "Cold chain management program", "Temperature testing", "Material testing", "Environmental packaging consulting", "BioDrain gel pack production", "Liner manufacturing", "Protective packaging fabrication", "Custom corrugated box cutting, printing, and styling"], "industries": ["Meal kit delivery", "Pharmaceutical distribution", "Pharmaceutical manufacturing", "Protective packaging", "Construction", "Temperature-sensitive distribution", "Packaging industry"], "materials": ["Expanded polystyrene (EPS)", "Biodegradable EPS", "Non-toxic gel pack formulations", "Reusable and recyclable gel pack materials", "Environmentally friendly liners", "BioDrain gel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and privately held leadership", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "140,000 sq ft headquarters facility with five to seven additional U.S. manufacturing plants", "Signature BioDrain environmentally safe disposal gel pack", "National manufacturing footprint for cold chain logistics"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Shelbyville, KY -> db, /about-us, /about", "Family-owned and privately held -> /about-us, /about", "140,000 sq ft facility on 26 acres -> /about-us, /about", "5-7 additional manufacturing facilities across US -> /about-us, /about", "300 employees -> /about", "300 customers -> /about", "34 years in business -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> /quality, /about", "Products: EPS, gel packs, liners, BioDrain -> /, /about-us, /about", "Industries: meal kit, pharmaceutical, packaging, construction, protective packaging -> /, /about-us, /about", "Cold chain management services -> /", "Temperature testing, material testing, environmental services -> /about", "Leadership names (Kevin Lyons, James Lyons, Ryan Usher, Billy Williams, Kassie Snyder, Ken Rocheck) -> /about", "Custom packaging solutions -> /, /about-us, /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "with a 140,000-square foot manufacturing facility", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "300", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='creative-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Creative Steel operates from Salem, Oregon, where it manufactures drivetrain and suspension components for the automotive aftermarket. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

Parts are produced from anodized 6061 aluminum with grade-zinc hardware, and are designed to replace specific OEM part numbers from Mercedes and General Motors.

The product line is narrow but targeted, with each mount engineered for a specific chassis and powertrain combination.

