UPDATE companies SET description='Creative Werks Inc. was founded in 2003 by the Folkestad family in Des Moines, Iowa. The family-owned business began as an electronic engineering firm focused on RF and embedded controls for off-highway and utility vehicles, and has since expanded into a full-service design, engineering, and manufacturing operation.

The company designs, engineers, and produces a wide variety of electronic control systems entirely in-house at its Des Moines facility. Its capabilities span RF control systems, custom embedded electronics, electromechanical engineering, and wireless RF solutions. A full machine shop supports production with 5-axis and 3-axis CNC mills, dual-spindle lathes with bar feeders, and dual SMT pick-and-place machines for circuit board assembly. Creative Werks reports an annual output of roughly 65,000 systems, with capacity to double that volume. It also stocks off-the-shelf controllers — 4, 6, and 75-channel remotes, linear actuators, and basic control units — ready for immediate shipment.

Creative Werks serves off-highway, agricultural, industrial, mobile, and automotive markets, as well as prototyping and custom projects. Notable public projects include the Foxzilla vehicle build, the Josh Robinson tool cart, the Spool Rule, and wiring for Jeff Lutz’s 57-foot dragster. Customers range from OEMs needing custom embedded controls to aftermarket performance shops seeking PWM fan controllers and RF remote systems.

The company emphasizes total control over design, engineering, and production as its differentiator, maintaining quality through every step. Its combination of an engineering team and a fully equipped machine shop allows it to develop solutions that would otherwise require multiple vendors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["RF control system design", "Custom embedded electronics development", "Electromechanical engineering", "In-house SMT circuit board assembly", "CNC milling (5-axis and 3-axis)", "CNC turning with live tooling and bar feeders", "Wireless RF solutions", "Off-the-shelf control units (4, 6, 75 channel)", "Linear actuator integration", "UI/UX design for embedded products", "Prototyping and product development", "U.S. manufacturing"], "industries": ["Off-highway", "Agricultural", "Industrial", "Mobile", "Automotive", "Utility vehicles", "Prototyping", "Custom"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["HAAS VF4 SS with 4th axis rotary", "HAAS VF3SS with 5-axis trunnion table", "HAAS ST20Y with dual spindles, live tooling, bar feeder", "HAAS ST20Y with live tooling, bar feeder", "HAAS TL2 Lathe", "Two Bridgeport manual mills", "Dual SMT pick and place machines"], "volume": "65,000 systems per year, capacity to double", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full in-house design, engineering, and production under one roof", "Machine shop with 5-axis/3-axis mills and dual-spindle lathes with bar feeders", "Dual SMT pick-and-place lines for circuit board assembly", "Annual production of 65,000 systems with capacity to double", "Off-the-shelf RF controllers (4, 6, 75 channel) in stock for immediate shipment"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2003 by the Folkestad Family -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Des Moines, IA -> /about-us, /", "Family-owned -> /about-us", "Produces ~65,000 systems annually with capacity to double -> /", "Specializes in RF and embedded controls for off-highway and utility vehicles -> /about-us", "In-house machine shop with HAAS VF4, VF3SS, ST20Y, TL2, Bridgeport mills, and dual SMT pick-and-place machines -> /about-us", "Offers off-the-shelf 4, 6, and 75-channel remotes, linear actuators, and control units -> /", "Serves off-highway, agricultural, industrial, mobile, automotive, prototyping, and custom markets -> /, /about-us", "Notable projects: Foxzilla, Josh Robinson Tool Cart, Spool Rule, Jeff Lutz 57'' Wiring -> /", "Total control of design, engineering, and production as differentiator -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Creative Werks Inc. is an electronics engineering and manufacturing company based in Des Moines, IA.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='creative-werks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Creekside Welding and Fabrication LLC operates from Bowman, South Carolina, serving Orangeburg and Dorchester counties. The company has been in business for over five years, offering welding, steel design, and fabrication services to the region.

The shop provides a range of metalworking services including MIG, TIG, and stick welding; mobile welding for on-site repairs; plasma cutting; custom steel fabrication; CAD drawing and design; repair of construction, forestry, and farm equipment; steel demolishing; and steel building sales and erection.

Its customer base spans construction, forestry, and agricultural sectors, along with commercial, industrial, and residential clients. The company''s SCDOT welding certification allows it to work on government and large-scale infrastructure projects, and its mobile unit travels to job sites and remote farm locations.

Creekside emphasizes its combination of modern CAD technology with traditional welding craftsmanship, a commitment to safety and quality, and a mission to exceed customer expectations through reliable, locally focused service.', certifications=ARRAY['SCDOT Welding Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Stick welding", "Mobile welding", "Plasma cutting", "Custom steel fabrication", "Steel design", "CAD drawing and drafting", "Construction equipment repair", "Forestry equipment repair", "Farm equipment repair", "Steel demolishing", "Steel building erection", "Steel building sales", "SCDOT-certified welding"], "industries": ["Construction", "Forestry", "Agriculture", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Residential", "Government"], "materials": ["Steel", "Metal"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["SCDOT-certified welding for government and infrastructure projects", "Mobile welding unit for on-site repairs at construction sites and farms", "In-house CAD drawing and design for precise fabrication planning", "Steel building sales and professional erection services", "Over five years of experience serving Orangeburg and Dorchester counties"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bowman, South Carolina -> db", "Service area: Orangeburg County, Dorchester County -> /about-us", "Over five years in business -> /about-us", "Services: welding (MIG, TIG, stick), mobile welding, plasma cutting, custom fabrication, steel design, CAD drawings, equipment repair, steel demolishing, steel building erection and sales -> /services", "Industries served: construction, forestry, agricultural, commercial, industrial, residential, government -> /about-us, /services", "Certification: SCDOT Welding Certified -> /about-us", "Differentiators: SCDOT certification, mobile welding, CAD drawings, steel building sales/erection -> /services", "Mission: provide unmatched quality and service exceeding expectations -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "From custom steel fabrication and CAD drawings to mobile welding and equipment repair, our experienced team is equipped to handle projects of all sizes and complexities.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='creekside-welding-and-fabrication-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cristek Interconnects was founded in 1985 in Anaheim, California, by 23-year-old Cristi Cristich. Armed with a $25,000 contract from Litton, a fistful of credit cards, and a small loan from her first boss, she launched the company to serve the military and aerospace industries. Today, the business operates as a Qnnect Company with manufacturing facilities spanning Southern California, New England, and Northern Nevada.

The company designs and manufactures micro-miniature and nano-miniature connectors, complex cable and harness assemblies, twist capsules, precision mechanisms, hermetic assemblies, RF/microwave components, and machined parts. Its vertically integrated operation covers DC through 67 GHz RF frequency connector, cable, and electromechanical design and assembly. Cristek employs over 100 people across more than 56,000 square feet of production space.

Cristek serves aerospace, defense, and space programs, supplying prime contractors and other customers with mission-critical interconnects for harsh environments including vibration, temperature extremes, and vacuum. Its products are used in applications where failure is not an option, such as satellite constellations, laser communication terminals, and other high-reliability platforms.

Cristek differentiates itself through vertical integration, engineering expertise in nanominiature and microminiature connector technology, and the ability to add EMI filtering and hermetic sealing to custom high-speed, matched-impedance solutions. The company emphasizes process discipline, metric-based management, and rapid prototyping to accelerate development cycles while maintaining rigorous standards.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100:2016','ISO 9001:2015','NADCAP AC7121','IPC 620','IPC JSTD','MIL SPEC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Micro-miniature connector manufacturing", "Nano-miniature connector manufacturing", "Complex cable assembly", "Harness assembly", "Twist capsule assembly", "Precision machining", "Hermetic sealing", "EMI filtering", "RF/microwave connector design", "High-speed matched-impedance design", "Rapid prototyping", "Vertical integration", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "Precision mechanisms", "Filter connector manufacturing", "D-subminiature connector manufacturing", "Circular connector manufacturing", "FilConn product manufacturing"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Space", "Military"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated design and manufacturing from DC to 67 GHz RF", "Expertise in nanominiature and microminiature connector technology", "EMI filtering and hermetic sealing for custom high-speed interconnects", "Rapid prototyping and flexible manufacturing for accelerated development", "Process-disciplined, metric-based quality management"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1985 by Cristi Cristich -> /about", "Headquarters Anaheim, California -> db", "Over 100 employees, 56,000 sq ft across Southern California, New England, Northern Nevada -> /about", "Certifications: AS9100:2016, ISO 9001:2015, NADCAP AC7121, IPC 620, IPC JSTD, MIL SPEC -> /", "Products: micro/nano connectors, cable assemblies, twist capsules, hermetic assemblies, RF/microwave, machined components -> /", "Industries: aerospace, defense, space -> /", "Part of Qnnect Company since 2023 acquisition -> /", "Vertical integration, DC to 67 GHz RF capability -> /about", "Rapid prototyping, flexible manufacturing -> /", "Woman founder (Cristi Cristich) -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "designing and manufacturing micro-miniature and nano-miniature connectors, complex cable assemblies, twist capsules and mechanisms", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "over 100", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/cristek/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cristek-interconnects' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Crossroads Fine Woodworking is preparing to open its doors in Marion, Indiana. The company has announced a grand opening and is promoting reduced membership fees for a limited time, though no founding year, ownership structure, or founder names have been disclosed.

The business operates as a retail outlet and community workshop, selling woodworking supplies, lumber, and providing shared workshop access through membership programs. Its inventory spans sanding discs and abrasives, orbital sanders, dust extraction systems, pocket-hole jigs, clamp systems, measuring tools, carving tool sets, and basswood blanks.

The company has not publicly stated a founding mission or explicit differentiator beyond its dual retail-and-workshop model, which aims to provide both the tools and the space to use them.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail sales of woodworking tools and supplies", "Lumber sales", "Community workshop access", "Membership programs"], "industries": ["Woodworking"], "materials": ["Lumber", "Basswood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Community workshop access via membership", "Curated selection of premium woodworking brands", "Combined retail and shared workspace model"], "facts_used": ["Location: Marion, Indiana -> db", "Grand opening coming soon -> /", "Reduced membership fees for limited time -> /", "Offers woodworking supplies, lumber, community workshop access -> /", "Sells products from brands including Kreg and Festool -> /", "Product listings include abrasives, sanders, dust extractors, jigs, clamps, carving tools, basswood blanks -> /", "No founding year, ownership, founders, employee count, certifications, or equipment stated -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Woodworking Supplies, Lumber, & Community Workshop Access", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='crossroads-fine-woodworking' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Crossroads Solar operates from South Bend, Indiana, where it was founded on the principle of maximizing three core values with a unique twist. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure, and no founders are named in public materials. Its facility sits near the Indiana Toll Road, linking the operation to Chicago, Detroit, and broader Midwest logistics networks.

The company manufactures monocrystalline solar panels in 60-cell and 72-cell configurations, and provides product testing and certification services. Its panels carry a 10-year product warranty. Details on facility size, headcount, or production volumes are not publicly available.

The business was started on the idea that a company can balance three priorities—referred to as the three P''s—though the specific priorities are not elaborated in available sources.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Monocrystalline solar panel manufacturing (60-cell and 72-cell)", "Product testing", "Certification services"], "industries": ["Solar energy"], "materials": ["Monocrystalline silicon"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Local pickup available", "National shipping via FPO", "Product testing and certification", "10-year product warranty"], "facts_used": ["Location: South Bend, Indiana -> db", "Facility address: 1901 N Bendix Dr, South Bend, IN 46628 -> /", "Products: 60-cell and 72-cell monocrystalline solar panels -> db", "Product testing and certification services -> db", "10-year product warranty -> db", "Local pickup and national shipping via FPO -> /", "Sourcing from local industries where possible -> db", "Founded on idea of maximizing three P''s -> db", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Crossroads Solar''s signature products include our 60 and 72 cell series of monocrystalline panels", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/crossroads-solar/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='crossroads-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Crown Wire & Cable Co. Inc. was founded in 1986 in Millville, New Jersey, located in the Millville Airport complex about 30 miles south of Philadelphia. The company began as a supplier to the oil, gas, and water industries and has grown into one of the largest stocking distributors of steel wire rope and submersible pump cable in the United States.

The company stocks a broad range of products including submersible pump cable in multiple constructions (flat jacketed, neoprene, PVC twisted, flat parallel, round double jacketed), steel wire rope in various configurations (6x7 sand line, 6x21 drilling line, 19x7 rotation resistant, 6x36 winch cable, 6x25 casing/tubing line, 6x19 rotary drill line), galvanized and Type 304 stainless steel aircraft cable, and manila rope. It also sources related electrical products such as URD, SER, overhead, triplex, quadraplex, and irrigation cables on request. Crown Wire ships nationwide and serves international markets in Central America, South America, and the Caribbean.

Crown Wire emphasizes 24/7 availability, with dedicated personnel reachable around the clock to handle inquiries and track shipments.

