UPDATE companies SET description='Crystal Farms Dairy Co. is headquartered in Edina, Minnesota. The company''s roots trace to the 1920s when Nathan Friedell founded Nathan''s Produce Company, and to the 1930s when Julius Rosenberg started an egg business after immigrating from Russia. The two operations merged in the 1970s, creating the Crystal Farms brand that sells cheese and other dairy products today.

The company produces a wide range of dairy items including shredded, block, sliced, and snack cheeses, ricotta, specialty cheeses, cream cheese, butter, English muffins, and bagels. Crystal Farms states that it sources its dairy from the Midwest and emphasizes a quality process that runs from ingredient selection through finished‑product inspection.

The brand also engages with community partners: it supports the national FFA organization and its Minnesota, Wisconsin, and Iowa chapters; donates products quarterly to the Ronald McDonald House; and supplies nearly all cheese and butter for All Square, a Minneapolis non‑profit grilled‑cheese shop that employs formerly incarcerated individuals.

